# Tracked example env for the /_ds design-system harness. Committed on purpose.
#
# The specimen route touches no Supabase and no auth, but it renders inside the
# app shell, and src/supabase.js throws at module load without a URL and a key.
# These placeholders exist only so that client can be constructed. They point at
# a port nothing listens on, so nothing can reach a real project by accident.
#
# Expect one ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED line in the console from the placeholder
# URL. It is harmless: getSession() resolves locally to "no session", and /_ds
# is let through both gates in dev.
#
# Boot it with:  npm run ds:dev      (vite --mode dsspec)
# Then open:     http://localhost:5175/_ds
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54329
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=dsspec-placeholder
